FROM cgr.dev/chainguard/wolfi-base:latest@sha256:1c451d46a0d5c4e9f2b38e0e8d3e299564a1aa95c21973efcc1980a9d1d2e73e

# CACHEBUST busts the apk layer cache each run so daily rebuilds pick up package updates
ARG CACHEBUST=unset
# Pin to the README-promised Go 1.26 line via the wolfi go-1.26 package (rather than
# chainguard/go:latest, which tracks the newest Go and silently moved to 1.27).
# Relax the exact /etc/apk/world pins first so "apk upgrade" actually applies security
# updates (the "=[0-9]" anchor leaves fuzzy "=~" pins alone).
RUN echo "cachebust=${CACHEBUST}" && \
    sed -i -E 's/=[0-9].*$//' /etc/apk/world && \
    apk update && apk upgrade --no-cache && \
    apk add --no-cache go-1.26

USER nonroot
WORKDIR /workspace

# Extract Go version information and save to /tmp/versions.txt
SHELL ["/bin/sh", "-o", "pipefail", "-c"]
RUN go version > /tmp/go_version.txt && \
    GO_VERSION=$(go version | cut -d' ' -f3 | sed 's/go//') && \
    echo "go=${GO_VERSION}" > /tmp/versions.txt && \
    GO_MAJOR=$(echo "${GO_VERSION}" | cut -d'.' -f1) && \
    GO_MINOR="${GO_MAJOR}.$(echo "${GO_VERSION}" | cut -d'.' -f2)" && \
    echo "go_major_tag=${GO_MAJOR}" >> /tmp/versions.txt && \
    echo "go_minor_tag=${GO_MINOR}" >> /tmp/versions.txt && \
    head -6 /tmp/versions.txt
